<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haakon VI of Norway</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1340">1340</a>–<a href="/years/1380">1380</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haakon VI was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> from 1343 to 1380 and also king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> from 1362 to 1364. He married Margaret, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-iv-of-denmark">Valdemar IV of Denmark</a>, in 1363, and their son Olaf inherited both <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and Norway. After the deaths of Haakon and Olaf, Margaret united the three Nordic crowns in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar-union">Kalmar Union</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haakon-vi-of-norway.jpg" alt="Haakon VI of Norway" width="287" height="338" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Drawing by Hakon Thorsen (d. before 1924) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kong_Haakon_VI_Magnusson_PI_XVII_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
